        },
        "text_P3dm3f": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Simran Design was commissioned to design a dedicated audio and video podcast studio for Darbar Arts & Heritage Trust at their new headquarters in Hayes, London.</p><p>The brief was to create a highly practical and adaptable recording environment that could be used both by the Trust and by external organisations hiring the studio. Flexibility was therefore a key consideration throughout the design process.</p><p>To achieve this, we developed a neutral, contemporary palette paired with colour-changing commercial LED lighting, allowing the studio to easily adapt to different brand identities and recording styles.</p><p>The result is a refined and versatile podcast space designed to support professional audio and video production, while remaining visually engaging on camera and comfortable for hosts and guests alike.</p>",
            "text_size": 3,
            "text_style": "font-body",
            "padding_bottom": 16
          }
        }
